Chapter: CheckSidecarsScript

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Shell chapter ShellTypes
  cites Shell chapter ShellBuild
  cites Shell chapter Pipeline
  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit

 We say:

 THE EIGHTEENTH GENERATOR ON THE PIPELINE MODEL (PipelineModel.md). The emitted
 script is byte-identical to the one that shipped before the migration.

 THIS ONE CHECKS TWO UNRELATED THINGS AND THE STAGES NOW SAY SO. Sidecars
 pointing at no test and `.expected` files without a trailing newline are
 separate defects with separate refusals, and both were previously readable
 only by following the control flow to the end. Each is a stage with its own
 verdict here.

Section: Parameters

  cs-default-root : ShellExpr = SePathJoin (SePathParent SeScriptRoot) (SeLit "codex/test")

  cs-params : List ShellParam = [sh-param-default "TestRoot" SptString cs-default-root]

Section: The pipeline, declared before it is spelled

  exts-list : List ShellExpr = [SeLit ".skip", SeLit ".slow", SeLit ".fatal", SeLit ".expected", SeLit ".stdin", SeLit ".keys", SeLit ".disk", SeLit ".disk2", SeLit ".disk-src", SeLit ".failing", SeLit ".diag", SeLit ".smp", SeLit ".vmargs", SeLit ".no-cross", SeLit ".covers", SeLit ".cross-refusal", SeLit ".cross-budget"]

  exts-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "exts", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "exts", pa-from = Just (SeArrayLiteral exts-list) }

  orphans-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "orphans", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "orphans", pa-from = Just (SeArrayLiteral []) }

  checked-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "checked", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "checked", pa-from = Just (SeInt 0) }

  noeol-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "noeol", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "noeol", pa-from = Just (SeArrayLiteral []) }

  exp-checked-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "expChecked", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "expChecked", pa-from = Just (SeInt 0) }

  all-files-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "allFiles", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "allFiles", pa-from = None }

  cs-arts : List PipeArtifact = [exts-art, orphans-art, checked-art, noeol-art, exp-checked-art, all-files-art]

Section: S01 -- Why this exists

  cs-doctrine : List ShellCmd = [ScComment "A sidecar names a test. This asserts the test exists.", ScComment "", ScComment "test.ps1 resolves every sidecar next to its source: for codex/test/apps/", ScComment "foo.codex it looks for codex/test/apps/foo.skip, and a foo.skip one", ScComment "directory up is read by nothing. Such a file is not inert -- it reads like", ScComment "a decision. diagnostic-boot carried a .skip in the wrong directory saying", ScComment "\"blocks waiting for keyboard input\"; the skip applied to nothing, the test", ScComment "was compiled but never run because it had no .expected, and the reason was", ScComment "wrong anyway (the shell reads serial, not the keyboard). Three claims, none", ScComment "true, and the skip inventory in docs/ExaminersAssay.md quoted it as a", ScComment "legitimate skip for months.", ScComment "", ScComment "db-mini-test.skip was the same shape with no test at all behind it: the", ScComment "only record of a real CDX2000 defect was a sidecar for a .codex that has", ScComment "never existed in main. That gap is recorded in docs/ExaminersAssay.md,", ScComment "named by the chapter it is actually in.", ScComment "", ScComment "Exit 1 on any sidecar whose .codex sibling is missing."]

  s01 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "doctrine", ps-why = "what a misplaced sidecar cost twice, and why an inert-looking file is a claim", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = cs-doctrine }

Section: S02 -- The sidecar extensions

  s02-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScSetStrictMode, ScSetErrorStop, ScBlank, pipe-produce exts-art, pipe-produce orphans-art, pipe-produce checked-art, pipe-produce noeol-art, pipe-produce exp-checked-art]

  s02 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "the sidecar extensions", ps-why = "the seventeen suffixes that configure a test, and the two findings lists", ps-in = [], ps-out = [exts-art, orphans-art, checked-art, noeol-art, exp-checked-art], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s02-body }

Section: S03 -- Every sidecar wants a .codex beside it

  cs-repo : ShellExpr = SePathParent SeScriptRoot

  cs-relative : ShellExpr = SeSubstringFrom (SeProperty (SeVar "f") "FullName") (SeAdd (SeTextLength cs-repo) (SeInt 1))

  cs-sibling : ShellExpr = SePathJoin (SeProperty (SeVar "f") "DirectoryName") (SeConcat (SeProperty (SeVar "f") "BaseName") (SeLit ".codex"))

  cs-check-one : List ShellCmd = [ScIncrement "checked", ScAssign "sibling" cs-sibling, ScIf (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "sibling"))) [ScAppend "orphans" cs-relative] []]

  cs-of-ext : ShellExpr = SePipe (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "allFiles") [StWhere (SeStringEq (SeProperty SeItem "Extension") (SeVar "ext"))]

  s03-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScAssign "allFiles" (SeAsArray (SeListFiles (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "TestRoot") "*" True)), ScForEach "ext" (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "exts") [ScForEach "f" cs-of-ext cs-check-one]]

  s03 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "every sidecar wants a .codex beside it", ps-why = "a sidecar is resolved next to its source, so one in the wrong directory configures nothing while reading like a decision", ps-in = ["TestRoot", "exts"], ps-out = [all-files-art], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s03-body }

Section: S04 -- A .disk-src names a SECOND test

  cs-peer-note : List ShellCmd = [ScComment "A .disk-src names a SECOND test -- the one whose freshly compiled CDX becomes", ScComment "this test's disk -- so it has a second way to point at nothing. A typo there", ScComment "does not fail until a battery run, which is the expensive place to find it."]

  cs-peer-read : ShellExpr = SeIfElse (SeVar "peerRaw") (SeTrim (SeVar "peerRaw")) (SeLit "")

  cs-names-nothing : ShellExpr = SeConcat (SeProperty (SeVar "f") "Name") (SeLit " names no test")

  cs-names-missing : ShellExpr = SeConcat (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeProperty (SeVar "f") "Name") (SeLit " names '")) (SeVar "peer")) (SeLit "', and no ")) (SeConcat (SeVar "peer") (SeLit ".codex exists"))

  cs-peer-glob : ShellExpr = SeListFiles (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "TestRoot") "*.codex" True

  cs-peer-file : ShellExpr = SeConcat (SeVar "peer") (SeLit ".codex")

  cs-peer-found : ShellExpr = SeCount (SePipe cs-peer-glob [StWhere (SeStringEq (SeProperty SeItem "Name") cs-peer-file)])

  cs-peer-body : List ShellCmd = [ScAssign "peerRaw" (SeFileFirstLine (SeProperty (SeVar "f") "FullName")), ScAssign "peer" cs-peer-read, ScIf (SeStringEq (SeVar "peer") (SeLit "")) [ScAppend "orphans" cs-names-nothing, ScContinue] [], ScIf (SeIntEq cs-peer-found (SeInt 0)) [ScAppend "orphans" cs-names-missing] []]

  s04-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScSequence cs-peer-note, ScForEach "f" (SeListFiles (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "TestRoot") "*.disk-src" True) cs-peer-body]

  s04 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "a .disk-src names a second test", ps-why = "the second way a sidecar points at nothing, and the one that otherwise waits for a battery run to surface", ps-in = ["TestRoot"], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s04-body }

Section: S04b -- An .expected must end in exactly one newline

  cs-eol-note : List ShellCmd = [ScComment "An .expected with no trailing newline can never pass. test-run.ps1 writes", ScComment "($lines -join \"`n\") + \"`n\", so the actual always ends in one LF, and", ScComment "test.ps1 strips CR from the expected side only. LF is not one of the", ScComment "characters the culture-sensitive -eq ignores (SOH and NUL are, which is a", ScComment "separate and live hazard), so the mismatch is real and the test is simply", ScComment "unpassable. Three shipped that way in CL 15313 and sat red until a release", ScComment "battery found them: the failure is loud, but something has to be listening.", ScComment "Account in docs/ExaminersAssay.md, under the .expected recording rule."]

  cs-exp-last : ShellExpr = SeSubstringFrom (SeVar "txt") (SeSub (SeTextLength (SeVar "txt")) (SeInt 1))

  cs-eol-bad : ShellExpr = SeAnd (SeIntGt (SeTextLength (SeVar "txt")) (SeInt 0)) (SeStringNeq cs-exp-last SeNewline)

  cs-eol-body : List ShellCmd = [ScIncrement "expChecked", ScAssign "txt" (SeFileText (SeProperty (SeVar "f") "FullName")), ScIf cs-eol-bad [ScAppend "noeol" cs-relative] []]

  s04b-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScSequence cs-eol-note, ScForEach "f" (SeListFiles (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "TestRoot") "*.expected" True) cs-eol-body]

  s04b : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "an .expected must end in one newline", ps-why = "an unterminated .expected can never match, therefore the test is unpassable rather than merely failing", ps-in = ["TestRoot"], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s04b-body }

Section: S05 -- The verdict

  cs-fail-head : ShellExpr = SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "FAIL: ") (SeCount (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "orphans"))) (SeLit " orphaned sidecar(s) -- no .codex beside them:")

  cs-fail-body : List ShellCmd = [ScEcho cs-fail-head, ScForEach "o" (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "orphans") [ScEcho (SeConcat (SeLit "  ") (SeVar "o"))], ScEcho (SeLit "A sidecar next to no test configures nothing and asserts something."), ScEcho (SeLit "Move it beside its .codex, or delete it -- but if it records a real"), ScEcho (SeLit "defect, write the defect down beside the code it describes first."), ScExit (SeInt 1)]

  cs-noeol-head : ShellExpr = SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "FAIL: ") (SeCount (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "noeol"))) (SeLit " .expected file(s) with no trailing newline -- they cannot pass:")

  cs-noeol-body : List ShellCmd = [ScEcho cs-noeol-head, ScForEach "o" (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "noeol") [ScEcho (SeConcat (SeLit "  ") (SeVar "o"))], ScEcho (SeLit "test-run.ps1 always terminates the actual with one LF, so a sidecar"), ScEcho (SeLit "without one can never match. Re-record it through build/test-run.ps1"), ScEcho (SeLit "rather than appending a byte by hand -- the same rule catches the CR,"), ScEcho (SeLit "the HEAP: lines and the leading SOH."), ScExit (SeInt 1)]

  cs-ok-line : ShellExpr = SeConcat (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "sidecars ok (") (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "checked")) (SeLit " checked, 0 orphaned; ")) (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "expChecked")) (SeLit " .expected, 0 without a trailing newline)")

  s05-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScIf (SeIntGt (SeCount (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "orphans")) (SeInt 0)) cs-fail-body [], ScIf (SeIntGt (SeCount (pipe-ref cs-arts cs-params "noeol")) (SeInt 0)) cs-noeol-body [], ScEcho cs-ok-line, ScExit (SeInt 0)]

 THE ORPHAN REFUSAL WINS OVER THE NEWLINE ONE: a run with both defects reports
 the orphans and exits before the newline list is printed, so the second
 finding is invisible until the first is fixed.

  s05 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "verdict", ps-why = "refuse on orphaned sidecars, then on unterminated .expected files, then report both tallies", ps-in = ["orphans", "noeol", "checked", "expChecked"], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "at least one sidecar sits beside no .codex, or a .disk-src names a test that does not exist", PoExit 1 "at least one .expected file does not end in a newline and therefore can never match", PoExit 0 "every sidecar names a test and every .expected is terminated"], ps-body = s05-body }

Section: Assembly

  cs-pipe : Pipeline = Pipeline { pl-name = "check-sidecars", pl-doc = "A sidecar names a test. This asserts the test exists.", pl-params = cs-params, pl-stages = [PsStage s01, PsStage s02, PsStage s03, PsStage s04, PsStage s04b, PsStage s05] }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (emit-powershell (pipeline-to-shell cs-pipe))
  end

